:::text id=QyacN_kKd0 at=top-center width=86% height=144 preset=title align=left
# How it works
:::

:::code id=jUCC05YN8H at=left-half width=44% height=440 offsetX=0 offsetY=120 language=ts
const result = compute({
  source,
  options: { strict: true },
});
:::

:::text id=EqqOocJa53 at=right-half width=42% height=248 offsetY=144 preset=body
The function takes a source object and returns a derived value. Strict mode enables runtime type checks — useful in development but adds overhead.
:::
